-- Which rule a HENCE or LEST belongs to, when a rule is nested inside another
-- rule's HENCE or LEST without brackets (smucclaw/l4-ide#1068).
--
-- A nested rule keeps a HENCE or LEST written at its own clauses, and ends at
-- one written at the clauses of the rule it is nested in (the whole rule is in
-- doc/reference/regulative/consequences.md). Each #EVAL below prints the rule
-- with the nested rules bracketed, so this file's golden shows where every
-- HENCE and LEST landed. Before the fix, the outer LEST in the first four
-- rules was taken by the innermost rule.

DECLARE Person IS ONE OF Seller, Buyer
DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
  delivery
  cancel
  payment HAS amount IS A NUMBER

-- The issue's repro. The Buyer's own LEST (the 120 payment) stays with the
-- Buyer's first rule; the Seller's LEST, at the Seller's clauses, is the
-- Seller's.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`two levels` MEANS
  PARTY Seller
  MUST delivery
  WITHIN 3
  HENCE
    PARTY Buyer
    MUST payment 100
    WITHIN 7
    LEST
      PARTY Buyer
      MUST payment 120
      WITHIN 14
  LEST BREACH BY Seller

-- One level: an inner rule with no LEST of its own does not take the outer
-- LEST either. Under a MAY, taking it would turn an unused permission into a
-- breach.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`one level` MEANS
  PARTY Seller
  MUST delivery
  WITHIN 3
  HENCE
    PARTY Buyer
    MAY cancel
    WITHIN 7
  LEST BREACH BY Seller

-- Clauses indented under the head, the layout the EVERY pages use: the outer
-- rule's clause column is 9, not its head's 5.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`indented clauses` MEANS
    PARTY Seller
        MUST delivery
        WITHIN 3
        HENCE
            PARTY Buyer
                MUST payment 100
                WITHIN 7
        LEST BREACH BY Seller

-- A rule on the same line as its HENCE: the LEST on the next line, at the
-- outer rule's clauses, is the outer rule's.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`same line` MEANS
  PARTY Seller
  MUST delivery
  WITHIN 3
  HENCE PARTY Buyer MUST payment 100 WITHIN 7
  LEST BREACH BY Seller

-- The HENCE side: a HENCE at the nested rule's own clauses chains after the
-- nested rule, and the LEST at the outer clauses is still the outer rule's.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`hence chain` MEANS
  PARTY Seller MUST delivery WITHIN 3
  HENCE PARTY Buyer MUST payment 100 WITHIN 7
        HENCE PARTY Seller MUST delivery WITHIN 9
  LEST BREACH BY Seller

-- On ONE line, a later LEST still belongs to the rule on that line.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`one line inner lest` MEANS
  PARTY Seller
  MUST delivery
  WITHIN 3
  HENCE PARTY Buyer MUST payment 100 WITHIN 7 LEST BREACH BY Buyer
  LEST BREACH BY Seller

-- Indented past the middle rule's clauses (column 5), a LEST belongs to the
-- innermost rule, even at a column that matches no rule's clauses.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`between columns` MEANS
  PARTY Seller
  MUST delivery
  WITHIN 3
  HENCE
    PARTY Buyer
    MUST payment 100
    WITHIN 7
    LEST
      PARTY Buyer
      MUST payment 120
      WITHIN 14
     LEST BREACH BY Seller

-- Brackets reset the columns: a rule whose head sits mid-line after "(" may
-- write its clauses left of its head.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`bracketed mid-line head` MEANS
    (PARTY Seller
        MUST delivery
        WITHIN 3
        HENCE (PARTY Buyer
            MUST payment 100
            WITHIN 7
            HENCE FULFILLED)
        LEST BREACH BY Seller)

-- The outer rule's clauses hang right of its PARTY, and the nested rule is
-- written further left. Each LEST goes to the rule whose clauses it lines up
-- with: the first to the Buyer, the second to the Seller.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`nested rule left of hanging clauses` MEANS
  PARTY Seller
      MUST delivery
      WITHIN 3
      HENCE
    PARTY Buyer
    MUST payment 100
    WITHIN 7
    LEST BREACH BY Buyer
      LEST BREACH BY Seller

-- Both rules' clauses at one column: a LEST there is the nested rule's.
-- Brackets would give it to the outer rule.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`same column` MEANS
  PARTY Seller
    MUST delivery
    WITHIN 3
    HENCE
    PARTY Buyer
    MUST payment 100
    WITHIN 7
    LEST BREACH BY Buyer

#EVAL `two levels`
#EVAL `one level`
#EVAL `indented clauses`
#EVAL `same line`
#EVAL `hence chain`
#EVAL `one line inner lest`
#EVAL `between columns`
#EVAL `bracketed mid-line head`
#EVAL `nested rule left of hanging clauses`
#EVAL `same column`
